---
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
---

<ServiceLayout
  title="Pricing | Flat-Fee Estate Planning | Mesa Estate Planning"
  description="Mesa Estate Planning offers flat-fee estate planning with published average fee ranges. Core packages start at $2,300 for individuals and $2,800 for married couples. No hourly billing, no surprises."
  heroTitle="Clear pricing. Built for what you need."
  heroSubtitle="All new work is flat-fee, with prices confirmed after your free consultation. You know exactly what you're paying before you commit to anything."
  breadcrumbParent="About"
  breadcrumbParentUrl="/about"
>
  <div class="quick-answer">
    <div class="quick-answer-label">Quick Answer</div>
    <p>Mesa Estate Planning uses flat-fee pricing for all new estate planning work. We publish average fee ranges and provide all clients with a written fee schedule tailored to their unique plan. Your fee is quoted after a free 30-minute consultation once we understand your situation. You know the total before you agree to anything.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>How Our Pricing Works</h2>
    <p>We break our estate planning into two categories: <strong>Core Estate Planning</strong> and <strong>Complex Estate Planning.</strong> Below are average flat-fee estimates and add-on charges for Core Estate Planning — the situations we plan for most often. Complex Estate Planning is so fact-specific to each client that we do not have helpful average pricing data available. We are happy to discuss Complex Estate Planning at your consultation.</p>

    <p>Please note that these estimates are not a promise. We cannot quote a price over the phone or on our website because every plan is tailored to your unique needs. These figures reflect a starting point; prices can be quoted up or down depending on your situation.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Core Estate Planning</h2>

    <h3>Core Packages</h3>
    <p>Each core package includes: revocable living trust, pour-over wills, financial power of attorney, healthcare power of attorney / living will, certificate of trust, and deed transfer &amp; recording for your primary residence.</p>

    <div class="pricing-table-wrap">
      <table class="pricing-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Starting Fee</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Core Estate Documents — Married Couple</strong></td>
            <td class="pricing-fee"><strong>$2,800</strong></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Core Estate Documents — Single Individual</strong></td>
            <td class="pricing-fee"><strong>$2,300</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Standard Add-Ons</h3>
    <p>Tailored provisions and additional services added to your core package as needed.</p>

    <div class="pricing-table-wrap">
      <table class="pricing-table pricing-table-addons">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Service</th>
            <th>Estimated Fee / Range</th>
            <th class="pricing-notes-col">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>LLC Creation &amp; Operating Agreement</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$800 – $1,200</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Single LLC formation with custom operating agreement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Each Additional LLC &amp; Operating Agreement</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$400 – $750</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Per additional entity</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Each Additional Deed &amp; Recording</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$250 – $350</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Rental properties, vacation homes, etc. (+ county recording fees)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Blended Family Provisions &amp; Complexity</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$1,000 – $3,000</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Separate/marital property, prior-marriage children, prenup integration</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pet Trust</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$350 – $500</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Integrated or standalone pet trust provisions</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Special Needs Trust (Third-Party)</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$3,000 – $5,000</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">For beneficiaries with disabilities; first-party SNTs are Complex Planning</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Basic Asset Protection Trust</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$3,500 – $5,500</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Fact-specific irrevocable trust planning; quoted after consultation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Done-for-You Trust Funding Assistance</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$1,000 – $2,000</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Full retitling of assets and coordination with financial institutions</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Beneficiary Designation Review &amp; Coordination</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$300 – $500</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Retirement accounts, life insurance, TOD/POD accounts</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Digital Asset / Digital Legacy Provisions</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">Included (or $250)</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Planning for crypto, online accounts, and digital businesses</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Gun Trust (NFA Firearms)</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$500 – $750</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Arizona-compliant NFA firearms trust</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Trust Amendment or Restatement</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$650 – $2,500</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Updating an existing plan (complexity determines final fee)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Annual Plan Review / Maintenance Plan</td>
            <td class="pricing-fee">$350/review or $950/yr</td>
            <td class="pricing-notes">Annual check-in, minor amendments, life-event review</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Complex Estate Planning</h2>
    <p>Business Formation &middot; QSBS Planning &middot; Asset Protection Strategies &middot; Business Succession Planning &middot; Estate Tax Reduction Strategies &middot; Charitable Tax Planning &middot; Life Insurance Trust Planning &middot; Dynasty Trust Planning</p>
    <p>Complex Estate Planning is quoted after consultation. These engagements involve multiple layers of planning, specialized tax analysis, and ongoing coordination that make published pricing impractical. We are happy to discuss scope and fees at your <a href="/contact">free consultation</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Here's what to expect for a quote</h2>
    <p><strong>Step 1:</strong> You book a <a href="/contact">free consultation</a>. This takes about 30 minutes and costs nothing.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 2:</strong> We review your situation and prepare a written recommendation that explains what documents we're proposing and why.</p>
    <p><strong>Step 3:</strong> We quote a flat fee for the recommended plan. You see the total cost before you commit to anything.</p>
    <p>No hourly billing. No invoices that grow beyond the original quote. The fee covers the full process from drafting through signing, including revisions and funding guidance. Done-for-you funding assistance is also available for all clients for an additional fee.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <p>Every engagement includes the initial consultation, document drafting, a review period where you can request changes, the signing meeting with notarization, and written funding guidance for trust-based plans. We don't charge extra for phone calls, emails, or revisions during the process. Significant changes after work has commenced may require fee revisions. Complex Estate Planning services include additional deliverables and follow-ups.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-section">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-section">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Can you give me a rough range of what estate planning costs?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Core Estate Planning for a married couple starts at $2,800 and for a single individual starts at $2,300. Add-ons like LLC formation, blended family provisions, or asset protection trusts are priced separately. Complex Estate Planning — which includes business succession, QSBS, and tax strategies — is quoted after consultation because the scope varies significantly.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Do you offer payment plans?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>We can discuss payment arrangements during the consultation. We want to make sure cost isn't the thing that stops someone from protecting their family.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          What if my situation changes after the plan is signed?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Amendments and updates are quoted separately as needed, also at a flat fee. A trust amendment or restatement typically runs $650 – $2,500 depending on complexity. We recommend reviewing your plan after any major life event and every three to five years. Our annual maintenance plan ($350 per review or $950/year) covers regular check-ins and minor amendments.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">
          Are these prices guaranteed?
          <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>The figures on this page are average starting points, not promises. Every plan is tailored to your situation, and your actual fee may be higher or lower. You will receive a written fee quote after your free consultation — before you commit to anything.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</ServiceLayout>
